From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: ask for a 64 frame block ack window

b43 asks for a block ack window of B43_AMPDU_MAX_FRAMES, the 32 MPDUs
it puts in one A-MPDU. While one A-MPDU waits for its block ack, the
next may only use what is left of those 32, so A-MPDUs to a busy
station averaged 17-19 MPDUs. brcmsmac keeps 32 MPDUs per A-MPDU but
a window of up to 64 (AMPDU_TX_BA_MAX_WSIZE).

Ask for 64. The window still follows what the receiver answers, and
the block ack bitmap from the TX status already has 64 bits.

BCM43217 (RT-AC56U), OnePlus Nord 2 (2x2), TCP download on channel 6,
alternating modules: 90.9 Mbit/s mean over 8 runs against 84.4 (wl
7.14 on the same router: 92-95). Bytes per RTS (one per A-MPDU) from
25.5-26.5 kB to 27.7-32.3 kB; no block ack or TX status errors.

Signed-off-by: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
@@ -835,6 +835,8 @@ enum {
 
 /* Maximum number of MPDUs b43 puts in one A-MPDU */
 #define B43_AMPDU_MAX_FRAMES	32
+/* Block ack window asked for: room for the next A-MPDU while one awaits its BA */
+#define B43_AMPDU_BA_WINDOW	IEEE80211_MAX_AMPDU_BUF_HT
 /* Times an MPDU missing from a block ack is sent again */
 #define B43_AMPDU_RETRY_LIMIT	5
 
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -6318,7 +6318,7 @@ static int b43_op_ampdu_action(struct ie
 			ieee80211_sn_sub(params->ssn, 1);
 		bsta->baw_start[params->tid] = params->ssn;
 		bsta->baw_pending[params->tid] = 0;
-		bsta->ampdu_buf[params->tid] = B43_AMPDU_MAX_FRAMES;
+		bsta->ampdu_buf[params->tid] = B43_AMPDU_BA_WINDOW;
 		return IEEE80211_AMPDU_TX_START_IMMEDIATE;
 	}
 	case IEEE80211_AMPDU_TX_OPERATIONAL: {
@@ -6326,7 +6326,7 @@ static int b43_op_ampdu_action(struct ie
 
 		/*
 		 * The window is the reorder buffer the receiver answered
-		 * with, which may be smaller than the B43_AMPDU_MAX_FRAMES
+		 * with, which may be smaller than the B43_AMPDU_BA_WINDOW
 		 * b43 asked for. Frames are aggregated as they are queued.
 		 */
 		bsta->ampdu_buf[params->tid] =
@@ -6883,7 +6883,7 @@ static struct b43_wl *b43_wireless_init(
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORT_FAST_XMIT);
 	/* Room for the TX header in front of the frame (one DMA descriptor) */
 	hw->extra_tx_headroom = sizeof(struct b43_txhdr);
-	hw->max_tx_aggregation_subframes = B43_AMPDU_MAX_FRAMES;
+	hw->max_tx_aggregation_subframes = B43_AMPDU_BA_WINDOW;
 	hw->sta_data_size = sizeof(struct b43_sta);
 	hw->wiphy->interface_modes =
 		BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP) |
